WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.860
Welcome back.

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.520
Let's connect gravity on the ground with escape into space.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.040
Our planet is spherical, and we ignore rotation.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:14.580
Outside it, gravitational force is G times capital M times little m, divided

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.720
by radius squared.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.720
Divide by the test mass to get gravitational acceleration.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.340
Radius means distance from the centre, not height above the ground.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.240
At height h, radius is R plus h.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.640
Surface gravity is g zero.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.300
The gravity ratio is R divided by R plus h, all squared.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.800
Try a height equal to the planet's radius. Pause.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.283
The centre distance doubles, so gravity becomes one quarter of surface

00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:42.740
gravity.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:47.868
For height much smaller than R, the ratio is approximately one minus two h

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:48.100
over

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:48.340
R.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.760
Do not use that shortcut at height R.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:55.240
Inside a uniform density planet, outer spherical shells cancel their field.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.020
Enclosed mass grows as radius cubed, so gravity grows linearly with radius.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.620
At depth d, gravity is g zero times one minus d over R.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.560
For one quarter of surface gravity, solve one minus d over R equals one

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:09.780
quarter.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.080
The depth is three quarters of R.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.880
The outside height was R; same gravity, different locations.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.260
Real Earth has varying density, so the interior line is an ideal model.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.840
Now choose potential zero at infinity.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.580
Outside, potential V is minus G M over r.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:29.140
Potential energy is little m times V.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.922
Moving outward makes energy less negative: lifting from R to two R requires G

00:01:34.922 --> 00:01:34.987
M

00:01:34.987 --> 00:01:37.800
m over two R if initial and final speeds are zero.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.680
Constant g times m times h works only for small heights.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.740
Field and potential are different.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:48.140
Equal masses on opposite sides cancel their fields at the midpoint, but their

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.340
negative potentials add.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:55.213
Inside our uniform sphere, potential is minus G M times three R squared minus

00:01:55.213 --> 00:01:55.280
r

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.320
squared, divided by two R cubed.

00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:02.880
At the centre, field is zero but potential is minus three G M over two R.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.060
Finally, escape needs just enough energy to reach infinity with zero final

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:07.340
speed.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:12.020
One half m v squared minus G M m over r equals zero.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.120
Escape speed is the square root of two G M over r, independent of test mass.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.360
For a radial surface launch at half escape speed, kinetic energy is G M m over

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.660
four R.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.200
Total energy is minus three G M m over four R.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.220
At the highest point, speed is zero.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:33.740
Solving gives radius four R over three, hence height R over three.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.280
This assumes no drag or later propulsion.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.320
A nonradial orbit retains tangential speed at its turning point, so that last

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:42.680
step cannot be copied blindly.

00:02:43.104 --> 00:02:46.224
A satellite keeps falling, yet keeps missing the ground.

00:02:47.164 --> 00:02:48.904
Gravity changes the direction of its velocity.

00:02:49.564 --> 00:02:54.724
For a circular orbit, G M m over r squared equals m v squared over r.

00:02:55.364 --> 00:03:00.244
Cancel mass and one radius: circular speed is the square root of G M over r.

00:03:00.844 --> 00:03:05.784
Period is circumference divided by speed, giving two pi times the square root

00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:08.304
of r cubed over G M.

00:03:08.304 --> 00:03:10.624
Always add the planet's radius to the supplied height.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:15.784
Let's compare equal mass satellites at radii r and four r around the same

00:03:15.784 --> 00:03:16.064
planet.

00:03:16.664 --> 00:03:18.164
What happens to speed and period?

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:20.024
Pause.

00:03:20.024 --> 00:03:22.964
Speed halves because it scales as the inverse square root of radius.

00:03:23.924 --> 00:03:27.444
Period multiplies by eight because it scales as radius to the power three

00:03:27.444 --> 00:03:27.784
halves.

00:03:28.764 --> 00:03:31.264
Potential energy is minus G M m over r.

00:03:32.064 --> 00:03:37.324
Circular kinetic energy is positive G M m over two r, so total energy is

00:03:37.324 --> 00:03:39.164
negative G M m over two r.

00:03:39.164 --> 00:03:44.764
In the outer orbit, total energy is minus G M m over eight r.

00:03:44.764 --> 00:03:49.924
Subtract the inner value: the increase is positive three G M m over eight r.

00:03:49.924 --> 00:03:53.484
Raising an orbit requires energy even though its circular speed decreases.

00:03:54.304 --> 00:03:58.324
This difference is not a single burn instruction; actual transfers involve

00:03:58.324 --> 00:03:59.344
intermediate motion.

00:04:00.244 --> 00:04:03.504
Astronauts float because they and their spacecraft accelerate together.

00:04:03.504 --> 00:04:08.524
Gravity still acts, but a freely floating astronaut has nearly zero support

00:04:08.524 --> 00:04:08.904
force.

00:04:09.704 --> 00:04:13.545
A geostationary satellite needs a circular equatorial orbit in Earth's

00:04:13.545 --> 00:04:13.984
rotation

00:04:13.984 --> 00:04:18.304
direction with the sidereal period, approximately eighty six thousand one

00:04:18.304 --> 00:04:19.604
hundred sixty four seconds.

00:04:20.184 --> 00:04:22.104
A one day period alone is insufficient.

00:04:22.824 --> 00:04:24.504
Now extend the picture to an ellipse.

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:29.524
Kepler's first law places the attracting body at one focus, not the centre.

00:04:29.524 --> 00:04:32.744
The second law gives equal swept areas in equal times.

00:04:32.744 --> 00:04:33.484
Why?

00:04:34.104 --> 00:04:37.744
Gravity is central, so its torque about the attracting centre is zero.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:42.312
Angular momentum stays constant, and the areal rate is angular momentum

00:04:42.312 --> 00:04:42.684
divided

00:04:42.684 --> 00:04:44.124
by twice the orbiting mass.

00:04:44.804 --> 00:04:48.484
At nearest and farthest points, velocity is perpendicular to radius.

00:04:49.104 --> 00:04:53.024
Therefore nearest radius times nearest speed equals farthest radius times

00:04:53.024 --> 00:04:53.644
farthest speed.

00:04:54.284 --> 00:04:58.164
If the farthest radius is three times the nearest, the nearest speed is three

00:04:58.164 --> 00:04:59.204
times the farthest speed.

00:04:59.884 --> 00:05:02.064
Equal areas do not mean equal distances.

00:05:02.624 --> 00:05:07.564
Kepler's third law says period squared scales as semi major axis cubed for

00:05:07.564 --> 00:05:09.764
bodies around the same dominant central mass.

00:05:10.444 --> 00:05:14.656
With nearest radius R and farthest radius three R, the semi major axis is

00:05:14.656 --> 00:05:14.944
their

00:05:14.944 --> 00:05:16.984
average, two R.

00:05:16.984 --> 00:05:20.644
Compared with a circle of radius R, the period is two times the square root of

00:05:20.644 --> 00:05:20.924
two.

00:05:21.644 --> 00:05:26.584
Elliptical total energy is minus G M m over twice the semi major axis, giving

00:05:26.584 --> 00:05:28.704
minus G M m over four R here.

00:05:28.704 --> 00:05:32.364
Do not replace that axis by the changing instantaneous radius.

00:05:33.144 --> 00:05:36.244
These are ideal two body results with negligible satellite mass.

00:05:37.044 --> 00:05:40.884
Use the written lesson for additional steps, then test the radius, energy and

00:05:40.884 --> 00:05:41.808
model assumptions before trusting an answer.
